## Project commands

- Tests: {{#if vars.testCommand}}`{{vars.testCommand}}`{{else}}not configured yet{{/if}}.
- Other checks (lint, type check, build): {{#if vars.checkCommand}}`{{vars.checkCommand}}`{{else}}not configured yet{{/if}}.

When a command is not configured, find it (package scripts, Makefile, task runner, CI workflows),
confirm it with the user and save it for the whole team, for example
`{{dfl.cli}} vars set testCommand "<command>"` (or `checkCommand`, several checks chained with
`&&`). The value lands in `.df/config.json`: commit it with the task and note it in the brief. A
project without tests gets a test framework in its first increment; never skip the tests because
no command exists yet.
